WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
Before the 2012 Games, east London's
Lower Lea Valley was largely derelict,

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.710
polluted and inaccessible.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.790
Today it holds Queen
Elizabeth Olympic Park,

4
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.030
free to visit.

5
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.550
In Glasgow, a museum where the Kelvin
meets the Clyde presents the city's heavy

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.970
industries, like shipbuilding.

7
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.030
And in rural Powys, the Hay
Festival was dreamt up in 1987,

8
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.170
in the book town of Hay-on-Wye.

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.670
Closed factories, empty land.

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.610
So how does a place like this persuade
investors and visitors to come?

11
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.110
In this mission, you'll
see how councils compete,

12
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.990
with local plans, zones and science parks.

13
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.230
Then you'll meet groups who clash
over what to keep or change.

14
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.430
Your mission: explain how a place with
closed factories can win investors and

15
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.290
visitors.
